{"case_id":"C035","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry point","API protocol","configuration","input semantics","attack surface"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["ares_sconfig_append_fromstr","parse_nameserver_uri","ares_uri_parse_buf","ares_get_server_addr","ares_get_server_addr_uri"],"reason":"H0 only fuzzes DNS-name query construction through ares_create_query and DNS-message parsing/writing through ares_dns_parse and ares_dns_write. S1 adds a distinct nameserver-configuration URI protocol whose parsing and serialization are not reached by either harness. This surface accepts structured dns URIs, IPv4/IPv6 hosts and scopes, ports, and a tcpport query parameter, making malformed delimiters, encodings, numeric values, and parse/write round trips fuzz-worthy.","evidence":["ares_sconfig_append_fromstr now tries parse_nameserver_uri before the legacy parse_nameserver path for each configuration entry.","parse_nameserver_uri calls ares_uri_parse_buf, requires scheme \"dns\", splits an IPv6 link-local scope at '%', parses the host with ares_dns_pton, obtains the UDP port with ares_uri_get_port, and parses the \"tcpport\" query key with atoi.","ares_get_server_addr selects ares_get_server_addr_uri when server->tcp_port differs from server->udp_port, introducing URI serialization for production server configuration.","ares_get_server_addr_uri constructs a dns URI with ares_uri_set_scheme, ares_uri_set_host, ares_uri_set_port, ares_uri_set_query_key, and ares_uri_write_buf.","The new src/lib/util/ares_uri.c contains extensive URI component validation, percent-encoded input handling, path normalization, query storage through ares_htable_dict_t, parsing, and writing logic.","Neither H0 harness calls ares_sconfig_append_fromstr, ares_uri_parse_buf, ares_get_server_addr, or any ares_uri_* function; their fuzz inputs are consumed only as a query name or a DNS wire message."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated harness that feeds arbitrary bounded byte strings into ares_sconfig_append_fromstr and directly into ares_uri_parse_buf, exercises both ignore_invalid modes and legacy/URI fallback, and serializes successfully parsed configurations through ares_get_server_addr or ares_uri_write_buf. Include parse-write-parse round trips and seeds covering dns:// IPv4 and bracketed IPv6 hosts, '%' scopes, absent/extreme ports, tcpport parameters, duplicate query keys, percent encodings, fragments, userinfo, malformed brackets, and delimiter-heavy lists."}
